usage: train.py [-h] --arm {memory,adapter,full} --stream-manifest
                STREAM_MANIFEST [--student-dir STUDENT_DIR]
                [--teacher-dir TEACHER_DIR] [--memory-init MEMORY_INIT]
                [--site SITE] [--hidden HIDDEN] [--tokens TOKENS]
                [--seq-len SEQ_LEN] [--micro-batch MICRO_BATCH]
                [--grad-accum GRAD_ACCUM] [--lr LR]
                [--weight-decay WEIGHT_DECAY] [--warmup WARMUP]
                [--temperature TEMPERATURE] [--kl-weight KL_WEIGHT]
                [--grad-clip GRAD_CLIP] [--optimizer {adamw,adam8bit}]
                [--optim-block OPTIM_BLOCK]
                [--optim-numerics {stochastic,nearest,compensated}]
                [--optim-measure-every OPTIM_MEASURE_EVERY]
                [--allow-dense-optimizer] [--schedule {constant,cosine}]
                [--min-lr-ratio MIN_LR_RATIO] [--freeze-embedding]
                [--no-freeze-embedding] [--gradient-checkpointing]
                [--keep-checkpoints KEEP_CHECKPOINTS] [--seed SEED]
                [--log-every LOG_EVERY] [--collision-every COLLISION_EVERY]
                [--ckpt-every CKPT_EVERY] [--resume RESUME] --run-dir RUN_DIR
                [--vram-limit-gib VRAM_LIMIT_GIB]

Stage-2 training loop: frozen anchor, trainable memory, online teacher KL. The
core is frozen. Only the arm module (the memory or the parameter-matched dense
adapter) receives gradients. The objective is L = CE(student, next token) +
lambda * T^2 * KL(teacher_T || student_T) where the teacher distribution is
computed **online** on the same batch — no logit cache is built or read. `T`
and `lambda` are command-line values written into the run manifest before the
first step; they are not tuned here. Weight-update numerics are recorded too
(S42). A bf16 weight update below half an ulp rounds to zero under round-to-
nearest; `optim8bit` applies stochastic rounding by default and can be asked
for nearest or an error-compensation buffer. On measured steps the optimiser
reports the fraction of parameter elements left bitwise unchanged, beside the
round-to-nearest fraction and the sub-half-ulp fraction, and the run receipt
carries the peak-LR and minimum-LR records. Discipline recorded per run: * the
memory table is **not** in the active union; only the 8 rows read per token
are. The projections and the convolution are. `active_per_token` comes from
`memory.MemoryGeometry`, never from a parameter count; * the data order is the
pinned stream in order (no shuffling in the smoke); resume continues at the
recorded token offset, so a resumed run sees exactly the same tokens; * the
checkpoint carries the arm state, optimiser, step, offset, RNG states, the
stream hash and the config hash. `--resume latest` verifies the hashes before
loading; * every step logs loss, CE, KL, learning rate, tokens/s, peak
allocated and reserved VRAM, and (periodically) the measured distinct-identity
count.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --arm {memory,adapter,full}
  --stream-manifest STREAM_MANIFEST
  --student-dir STUDENT_DIR
  --teacher-dir TEACHER_DIR
  --memory-init MEMORY_INIT
  --site SITE
  --hidden HIDDEN
  --tokens TOKENS
  --seq-len SEQ_LEN
  --micro-batch MICRO_BATCH
  --grad-accum GRAD_ACCUM
  --lr LR
  --weight-decay WEIGHT_DECAY
  --warmup WARMUP
  --temperature TEMPERATURE
  --kl-weight KL_WEIGHT
  --grad-clip GRAD_CLIP
  --optimizer {adamw,adam8bit}
  --optim-block OPTIM_BLOCK
  --optim-numerics {stochastic,nearest,compensated}
                        weight-update rounding for the 8-bit optimizer
  --optim-measure-every OPTIM_MEASURE_EVERY
                        also measure unchanged-element fractions every N steps
  --allow-dense-optimizer
  --schedule {constant,cosine}
  --min-lr-ratio MIN_LR_RATIO
  --freeze-embedding
  --no-freeze-embedding
  --gradient-checkpointing
  --keep-checkpoints KEEP_CHECKPOINTS
                        keep only the newest N ckpt-*.pt files (0 keeps all)
  --seed SEED
  --log-every LOG_EVERY
  --collision-every COLLISION_EVERY
  --ckpt-every CKPT_EVERY
  --resume RESUME
  --run-dir RUN_DIR
  --vram-limit-gib VRAM_LIMIT_GIB
